# TypeScript Coding Standards

## Type Safety

- Use strict mode (enabled in [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json))
- Define explicit types for all API responses
- Use interfaces for object shapes
- Avoid `any` type - use `unknown` if needed

## API Integration

- Define types in [web/src/types.ts](mdc:web/src/types.ts)
- Use consistent naming for API endpoints
- Handle errors gracefully with proper error types
- Implement request cancellation for better UX

## Performance

- Use debouncing for search inputs (300ms)
- Implement virtual scrolling for large result sets
- Cache API responses when appropriate
- Use request cancellation to avoid race conditions

## Code Organization

- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Use utility functions in [web/src/utils.ts](mdc:web/src/utils.ts)
- Separate API logic in [web/src/search.ts](mdc:web/src/search.ts)
- Follow consistent naming conventions

## Example Patterns

```typescript
// API response typing
interface SearchResponse {
  results: SearchResult[];
  total: number;
  page: number;
  limit: number;
}

// Error handling
try {
  const response = await searchAPI.search(query);
  // handle success
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Search failed:', error);
  // handle error
}

// Request cancellation
const controller = new AbortController();
const response = await fetch(url, {
  signal: controller.signal
});
```

## Development Tools

- Use ESLint with TypeScript rules
- Enable Prettier for code formatting
- Use Vite for fast development builds
- Enable hot module replacement